# Contact-form delivery
# ===========================================================================
# The contact form sends inquiries to info@aimenansari.com via Web3Forms. A
# Web3Forms access key is already built into the code (public by design), so it
# works with nothing else to configure.
#
# If no key is ever present, the form still works by opening the visitor's mail
# client with the message pre-filled to info@aimenansari.com.
#
# You only need the variables below to OVERRIDE the built-in key or switch
# delivery to EmailJS. Whichever is filled in wins: Web3Forms first, then
# EmailJS, then the mail-client fallback.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OPTION 1 — Web3Forms (ACTIVE — a key is already built into the site)
#   The form currently delivers to info@aimenansari.com via Web3Forms using a
#   key embedded in the code (public by design). You only need to set the value
#   below if you want to OVERRIDE / ROTATE that built-in key.
#   Get a new key at https://web3forms.com (enter info@aimenansari.com).
#   Free tier: ~250 submissions / month.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=

# OPTION 2 — EmailJS (three values)
#   1. Create an account at https://dashboard.emailjs.com
#   2. Add an email service connected to info@aimenansari.com
#   3. Create a template with these variables in the body:
#        Name:         {{from_name}}
#        Email:        {{from_email}}
#        Reply to:     {{reply_to}}
#        Project type: {{project_type}}
#        Subject:      {{subject}}
#        Message:      {{message}}
#        To:           {{to_email}}      <-- the recipient
#   4. Copy the Service ID, Template ID and Public Key below.
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
